PROJECT NON-NEGOTIABLE: No static trading thresholds or magic market parameters.
Unless a number is a mathematical identity, exchange/protocol constraint,
accounting convention, or pure UI/cadence setting, it must not be a fixed
trading rule such as 8%, $500, 3 trades, or 0.25% NAV. Entry, exit, sizing,
profit harvest, replacement, derisk, stop, universe selection, throttling, and
capital allocation parameters must be dynamic variables derived from live or
learned market state: volatility, liquidity, cost, regime, signal edge,
portfolio exposure, broker constraints, position age, or audited model
evidence. If a numeric coefficient remains, document what it multiplies and why
it is dimensionless; if a fixed safety bound is unavoidable, document the
external reason. Treat any existing absolute trading threshold touched during a
task as technical debt to replace, not copy.
